OTLP/OTAP gRPC receivers: `max_connection_age` and `max_connection_age_grace`
(grpc-go's MaxConnectionAge / MaxConnectionAgeGrace), off by default.

gRPC clients re-resolve the server's name only when a connection closes, so
behind a DNS name that fans out to several receivers (a headless Service with
`dns:///` + round_robin agents), a receiver added by a scale-up gets no
traffic until the clients restart. With an age set, each connection is sent a
graceful GOAWAY at its age (jittered +/-10% per connection); the client moves
new RPCs to a new connection (re-resolving) and the in-flight ones finish.
The grace bounds how long they may take; after it the connection is closed.

- otap: `otap_grpc::connection_age`: `ConnectionAge` (validation, jitter),
  `serve_with_connection_age(server, routes, incoming, signal, age, observer)`,
  which with no age is exactly `server.add_routes(routes)
  .serve_with_incoming_shutdown(..)`. With an age, each accepted connection
  gets its own clone of the tonic `Server` whose shutdown signal fires at the
  connection's age, so tonic's own graceful-shutdown path sends the GOAWAY
  (h2's two-step: last-stream-id 2^31-1 + PING, then the real id) and waits
  for the in-flight RPCs. The grace is a deadline on the connection's I/O
  (`AgedIo`), which then fails reads/writes and hyper drops the connection
  (logged, and reported to the observer).
  tonic 0.14's own `Server::max_connection_age` is not usable: one age for
  every connection, no GOAWAY at all when a grace is set, and without one it
  re-polls its finished timer (panic: `async fn` resumed after completion),
  killing the connection's in-flight RPCs whenever it is busy at that moment.
- `GrpcServerSettings` gains the two humantime fields (serde default `None`)
  and `connection_age()` (validated in the OTLP receiver's `from_config`:
  grace needs an age, age > 0; a warning when grace <= `timeout`).
- OTLP receiver: builds `Routes` and serves through the helper; new metric
  set `receiver.otlp.connections` {aged_out, force_closed}.
- OTAP receiver: the same two config fields and helper (logs only).
- Tests: validation, jitter bounds, a raw-frame check of the two GOAWAYs at
  the age, in-flight RPC completes within the grace while a new one is
  refused, an RPC longer than the grace is cut and counted, no age = no
  change, shutdown still drains.

Not proposed upstream (otap-s3pq local patch).

